; Fleet clj-kondo config — copied byte-identical to
; .clj-kondo/config.edn in each adopted repo (see cljfmt.edn header
; for the sync law). v1 pins the tool floor and otherwise runs the
; clj-kondo DEFAULT linter levels: the Phase 1 census measures the
; default gate. Linter levels are never demoted to make a repo pass;
; off-by-default idiom linters are enabled in deliberate fleet-wide
; batches, recorded here.
{:min-clj-kondo-version "2026.10.26"
 ;; Repo-local addition (proposed to the fleet in RETRO.md): teach
 ;; kondo the two defining macros this codebase builds on. Without
 ;; this, every var they define reads as an unresolved symbol and
 ;; their bodies are not analyzed at all.
 ;;  cohost.pool/deftask  - defines one task var per pool task
 ;; (jolt.ffi/defcfn is NOT defn-shaped - its arg vectors carry type
 ;; specs - so it is taught by the analyze-call hook in
 ;; .clj-kondo/hooks/jolt.cljc instead.)
 :lint-as {cohost.pool/deftask clojure.core/defn}
 :hooks {:analyze-call {jolt.ffi/defcfn hooks.jolt/defcfn}}}
